meta {
  name: DeleteBestingBlocked
  type: http
  seq: 34
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/web/bon/{{bestingBonnr}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Auth-Token: {{authToken}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 409
  res.body.error.code: eq 409
}

docs {
  Attempts to delete a bon that has a bonlijn with besteld <> 0 - must
  409. Note: in this iteration, the existing "has related order
  lines/records" (HasChildRows) check fires first since the bonlijn row
  itself already blocks deletion, so this currently surfaces the generic
  child-rows message rather than the newer, more specific
  "has order lines with besteld <> 0" message
  (Luna.BusinessLogic.BonBE:HasOutstandingBestelling) - that guard is
  unreachable today by construction but kept per the approved design for
  when/if HasChildRows' bonlijn check changes independently. Either way
  the result is 409. Requires {{bestingBonnr}} to be set (run
  "DeleteBestingCreateBon" and "DeleteBestingSetup" first).
}
